// Package chat renders chat templates and parses what the model writes back
// (SPEC §2, §5): messages, tools and the thinking flag go in through the
// model's template; tool calls and the reasoning block come out through a
// per-family parser.
//
// The open question of SPEC §14 is settled for v1 by the single model: Gemma
// 4's template is written out in Go (gemma4.go) and held byte for byte to the
// template in the model's GGUF, rendered by jinja2 over a corpus of
// conversations (testdata, regenerated by tools/chatfixtures/gen.py). A Go
// Jinja engine waits for a second model family. The answer parser (parse.go)
// mirrors llama.cpp's Gemma 4 parser.
package chat
